     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"cost\": 5, \"rationale\": \"Entry footholds are free starting points, so they are not counted. The cheapest route needs 5 steps: h1_1:escalate (AND, both entries reached) -> h1_0:access (OR, from an entry) -> h2_2:reach (AND, needs h1_1, h1_0 and edge1, all reached) -> h4_0:traverse (OR, from h2_2) -> crown:obtain (OR, from h4_0). Two other routes tie at 5 steps: through h2_2 -> h4_2 -> crown, and through h1_1 + h2_1 (from edge0) -> h3_1 -> h4_1 -> crown. Any route through h2_0 needs h1_0, h1_1, h1_2 and h2_0 before the last two steps, which makes at least 6. No route needs fewer than 5, because crown's parents each sit at least two steps beyond the first-layer steps.\"}"
    }
